1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Chime

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Chime

3
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Chime

4
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:16,000
First off, what the heck are you blubbering about over there?

5
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:18,000
It's contagious.

6
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Well, stop it!

7
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:33,000
I... I washed it, so don't worry. It's not dirty. And it won't curse you.

8
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:37,000
That's not the issue. I know that.

9
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:44,000
Don't cry, it's annoying!

10
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:49,000
Tell me what happened between you and Kaze Haya.

11
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:54,000
I... I realized how much I liked him.

12
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Are you dating?

13
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:59,000
Did you tell him that you liked him? Did he tell you?

14
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:01,000
Huh?

15
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:03,000
Did I?

16
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Or did he?

17
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Of course not!

18
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Really? You two aren't going out?

19
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:10,000
No way that happened!

20
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:11,000
You don't know that!

21
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Like, what if he gets caught up in the moment?

22
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:17,000
He could totally ask you out!

23
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Wha... wait a minute...

24
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:26,000
Are you telling me there's a chance that Kaze Haya might like me back?

25
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Until a little while ago, I was a total loner who didn't even have a single person to talk to.

26
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:36,000
It doesn't matter. Kaze Haya wouldn't judge someone for that.

27
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:47,000
He's kind. And he looks after people.

28
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:51,000
And he... sees you for who you really are.

29
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:56,000
Yeah. And when he smiles, no matter what, you can't help but smile with him.

30
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Exactly! But also, if you mess up with something important, he'll hold you accountable!

31
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:01,000
Mm-hmm.

32
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:05,000
He's surprisingly short-tempered, and he just hates when people do the wrong thing!

33
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:08,000
Regardless of gender, everyone looks up to him!

34
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:10,000
He's honest... and cheerful... cute!

35
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:13,000
Why the heck am I sharing all this with you?!

36
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:19,000
I love this. I've never talked like this... with anyone before.

37
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:25,000
Despite the things Kurumi says, I can tell that she acknowledges me for who I truly am.

38
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:29,000
In that way, she's just like Kaze Haya.

39
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:33,000
Why'd this happen? It should've been perfect timing!

40
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:39,000
We started high school, and I even got everyone to support the idea of us being together!

41
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:44,000
Now was the time... to make him fall for me!

42
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:47,000
The perfect time!

43
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,000
But in the end, it was all for nothing!

44
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Earlier, I... accidentally made Kaze Haya think that I like Pin Arai!

45
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:56,000
Huh?!

46
00:03:56,000 --> 00:04:00,000
No matter what I say now, he'll probably assume I'm just denying it out of embarrassment!

47
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:06,000
How did that happen?!

48
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:08,000
I miscalculated, okay?!

49
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:11,000
I don't care anymore.

50
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,000
Kaze Haya was never interested in me.

51
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:16,000
Not in that way.

52
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,000
I already knew that.

53
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:23,000
Does it really matter if he finds out what I did, or thinks I like someone else?

54
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:26,000
Yes, it does.

55
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:27,000
Yes, it does.

56
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:32,000
I mean... I didn't want him to think I like Sanada.

57
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:34,000
It felt awful being misunderstood.

58
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:36,000
I understand.

59
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:38,000
So I'm sure he will too if you just talk to him.

60
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:44,000
You think that he'll understand everything as long as I just talk to him?

61
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:45,000
Are you stupid?

62
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:58,000
But still, I can tell, I don't think she would ever be happy leaving things like this.

63
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:03,000
I know I wouldn't be, and we share the same feelings for the same person.

64
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:05,000
We both love Kaze Haya.

65
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:09,000
But sharing the same feelings makes it difficult.

66
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:12,000
Is it really not possible for us to be friends?

67
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:17,000
And if we're not friends, then I wonder what that would make us.

68
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:20,000
Is there a word for it?

69
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:23,000
Are we nothing but strangers again?

70
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:27,000
Or maybe... something completely new and different?

71
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:29,000
Uh... Oh, there you are!

72
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,000
Huh?

73
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:32,000
Is your stomach okay?

74
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:34,000
Yeah, it's better now.

75
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:37,000
We got worried when you disappeared on us like that.

76
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:40,000
I'll be able to play in the games tomorrow, though.

77
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:42,000
Well, that's good at least.

78
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:43,000
Yeah!

79
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:44,000
See you tomorrow, then.

80
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:45,000
Okay?

81
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:46,000
Bye-bye!

82
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:47,000
Bye!

83
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:49,000
It's pretty late now.

84
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:50,000
Wanna hang somewhere?

85
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:52,000
In other words, you're hungry?

86
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:55,000
Karumi!

87
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:57,000
Let's be on the same team!

88
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:58,000
It'll be great!

89
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:00,000
Oh, hey!

90
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:03,000
What?!

91
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:04,000
No way!

92
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:06,000
You seriously don't have a crush on anyone?!

93
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:07,000
You're so cute!

94
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:08,000
What a waste!

95
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:13,000
I'm so glad we became such good friends!

96
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:14,000
Same here!

97
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:15,000
Right?

98
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:17,000
Being in the same circle is the best!

99
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:21,000
Huh?

100
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:22,000
No way!

101
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:24,000
Miyagawa said that he liked Karumi?

102
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:25,000
Seriously?

103
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:26,000
What the hell?

104
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:29,000
Miki's like Miyagawa for as long as I can remember!

105
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:32,000
Oh, she has been!

106
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:35,000
Learning Miyagawa her notebook and stuff like that!

107
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:40,000
She probably doesn't like it when any of the guys like a girl who isn't her!

108
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:43,000
She's just pretending to be interested!

109
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:44,000
That's awful!

110
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:47,000
Plus she called herself Karumi when her name's Ume!

111
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:51,000
I only let her into our group because I thought she'd make it easier for us to talk to the boys!

112
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:52,000
Hey guys!

113
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:55,000
If she ever has a real crush, we should ruin it for her!

114
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:57,000
She went out of her way to mess with us, so why not?!

115
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:58,000
Right?!

116
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:04,000
Hey, uh, you seem kinda... down lately...

117
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:06,000
No, I'm totally fine!

118
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:07,000
That's good!

119
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,000
See you tomorrow then!

120
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:09,000
Bye-bye!

121
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:10,000
Bye-bye!

122
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:11,000
Uh...

123
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:13,000
Practicing in the rain really sucks, though!

124
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:14,000
Wanna ditch?

125
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:15,000
You can't do that!

126
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:16,000
You're no fun!

127
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:17,000
Oh, hey!

128
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:19,000
You haven't gone home yet!

129
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:20,000
Something wrong?

130
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:21,000
Mm-mm...

131
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:22,000
It's nothing!

132
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:23,000
You sure?

133
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:24,000
Yeah!

134
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:25,000
You have practice, Kazehaya?

135
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:26,000
Mm-hmm!

136
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:27,000
I'm just grabbing something real quick!

137
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:28,000
Oh, I see!

138
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:29,000
Oh, I knew I left it here!

139
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:30,000
Good luck!

140
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:31,000
Thanks!

141
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:32,000
Thanks!

142
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:01,000
Thanks!

143
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:02,000
Uh...

144
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:03,000
Seriously...

145
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:04,000
You sure you're okay?

146
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:17,000
Whoa!

147
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:18,000
What is it?

148
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:25,000
He's so different.

149
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:28,000
He's popular and always surrounded by the other boys.

150
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:29,000
Same class again?

151
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:30,000
And yet...

152
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:33,000
He always sees me for who I am.

153
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:35,000
I won't tell anyone.

154
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:37,000
Not a single soul.

155
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:40,000
Nobody.

156
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:43,000
Not until...

157
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:47,000
The day Kazehaya falls for me.

158
00:08:47,000 --> 00:09:00,000
Oh, hey, it's you.

159
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:05,000
Oh, hey, it's you.

160
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:08,000
I had no clue.

161
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:13,000
That said, you don't care even if Kazehaya finds out about this.

162
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:15,000
I can't believe it.

163
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:18,000
You actually have a crush on Pin!

164
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:22,000
I don't!

165
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:23,000
Oh!

166
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:24,000
I'm sorry.

167
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:26,000
That's rude of me, right?

168
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:28,000
You haven't heard?

169
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:30,000
About?

170
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:32,000
Uh...

171
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:38,000
What's her deal?

172
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:39,000
She pisses me off.

173
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:41,000
Acting like a saint.

174
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,000
Kazehaya?

175
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:46,000
Hm?

176
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:49,000
What kind of person is Sawako?

177
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:50,000
Hmm...

178
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:55,000
Hmm...

179
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:57,000
Kuro Numa's easily misunderstood.

180
00:09:57,000 --> 00:10:01,000
But no matter how risky something might be, she always speaks the truth.

181
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:05,000
That's why, no matter what it is she tells me, I always believe her.

182
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:07,000
Risky?

183
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:09,000
Yeah.

184
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:11,000
She probably isn't aware of it, but...

185
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:18,000
If Kuro Numa were the type to always lay low and play it safe, I think it's possible even Yano and Yoshida wouldn't have fully believed her.

186
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:24,000
Even if we want to help her, she always ends up working things out herself.

187
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:25,000
That's just how she is.

188
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:29,000
She's really come a long way.

189
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:32,000
I understand.

190
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:35,000
So I'm sure he will, too, if you just talk to him.

191
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:38,000
What am I saying?

192
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:40,000
I sound so arrogant.

193
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:42,000
See ya.

194
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:44,000
Kazeh...

195
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:48,000
Cheer up, okay?

196
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:56,000
I didn't want Kazehaya to misunderstand.

197
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:59,000
I don't want him to misunderstand.

198
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:01,000
Please...

199
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:04,000
No...

200
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:05,000
Wait...

201
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:08,000
Kazehaya, wait!

202
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:11,000
You're wrong!

203
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:13,000
Pina isn't the person I like!

204
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:18,000
The one I really like is...

205
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:20,000
You, Kazehaya!

206
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:24,000
It was always you!

207
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:25,000
Only you!

208
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:29,000
Oh, Kazehaya...

209
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:33,000
Please stop thinking I like someone else!

210
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:35,000
I just can't...

211
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:37,000
I can't take it!

212
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:46,000
I'm so sorry about that.

213
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:48,000
Really.

214
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:50,000
I'm an idiot.

215
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:53,000
I'm sorry.

216
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:54,000
I know.

217
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:55,000
It's so obvious!

218
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:56,000
It's impossible...

219
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:57,000
For me to see anyone else but her.

220
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:58,000
So...

221
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:00,000
I'm sorry.

222
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:02,000
I know.

223
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:03,000
It's so obvious!

224
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:04,000
Kazehaya...

225
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:06,000
Kazehaya...

226
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:09,000
Kazehaya, does me telling you that I like you make you feel happy at all?

227
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:10,000
Yeah.

228
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:11,000
Yeah.

229
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:12,000
Thank you.

230
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:13,000
Thank you.

231
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,000
Just this once.

232
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:15,000
Call me by my name.

233
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:16,000
I know.

234
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:17,000
I know.

235
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:18,000
It's so obvious!

236
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:24,000
Kazehaya, does me telling you that I like you make you feel happy at all?

237
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:25,000
Oh?

238
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:26,000
Uh...

239
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:29,000
Yeah.

240
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:31,000
Thank you.

241
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:42,000
Just this once.

242
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:44,000
Call me by my name, okay?

243
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:46,000
My first name.

244
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:50,000
Ume.

245
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:59,000
Well, I suppose this granny name isn't as bad as I thought then.

246
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:02,000
Man, saying all this stuff wasn't my intention.

247
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:04,000
I really miscalculated.

248
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:06,000
Miscalculated?

249
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:09,000
The one who threw me off the most was...

250
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:12,000
Definitely you, Kazehaya.

251
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:17,000
Oh, you're making a huge mistake!

252
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:20,000
You'll never find a girl as cute as I am!

253
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:23,000
Also, how could you think I was into that idiot peen?

254
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:24,000
It's ridiculous!

255
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:27,000
There.

256
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:28,000
Much better.

257
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:29,000
That was...

258
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:31,000
Have you always been like this?

259
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:33,000
Kazehaya!

260
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:35,000
You have no eye for girls!

261
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:39,000
See ya!

262
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:44,000
Uh-oh.

263
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:46,000
I said it!

264
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:51,000
I can't help but wonder...

265
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:55,000
If we had liked different people...

266
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:59,000
Maybe we would've been able to understand each other better...

267
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:01,000
If only...

268
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:03,000
Huh?

269
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:04,000
Kazehaya?

270
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:05,000
Yes!

271
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:06,000
So I was right!

272
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:07,000
Oh, who'd've thought?

273
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:09,000
Wait, why are you playing dumb, Yanuchi?

274
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:10,000
And I thought it was embarrassing!

275
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:11,000
Uh, yeah, no reason.

276
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:13,000
Oh, really?

277
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:17,000
Hey, so did something happen that made you realize you liked him?

278
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:19,000
I guess...

279
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:20,000
It was...

280
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:21,000
